7. Before the trial, the nature, significance, possible benefits, possible inconvenience, potential risks and discomfort of the trial have been understood in detail, and they have volunteered to participate in the clinical trial. They can communicate well with researchers, comply with the requirements of the whole trial, and have signed a written informed consent.

Exclusion Criteria:

