7. Serious trauma, serious infection or operation that may affect blood glucose control occurred within 1 month before screening;
8. There are obvious blood system diseases (such as aplastic anemia, myelodysplastic syndrome), or any disease that causes hemolysis or red blood cell instability (such as malaria), or hemoglobinopathy that may affect the determination of HbA1c level (such as sickle cell disease);
